course: dictionary
lesson: 8862
title: The shopkeeper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shopkeeper is a person who owns or runs a small shop. The word is made of two parts: shop, and keeper, which means someone who looks after something. So a shopkeeper looks after a shop.
explain: Context gives you the clues. «Harry said sorry to the shopkeeper and paid with his own pocket money.» Harry pays, so the shopkeeper must be the person he pays in the shop, who sells things.
explain: Shopkeepers also buy stock, set prices and give change. In a story, «a kind or grumpy shopkeeper» tells you how the person behaves, not what their job is. The word kind or grumpy is a clue to their character.
fact: A shopkeeper is a person who owns or runs a small shop.
fact: Shopkeeper is a noun. Its plural is shopkeepers.
fact: A shopkeeper buys stock, sets prices and gives you change when you pay.
fact: Each sale takes one thing off the shelf and brings money into the shop.
fact: In the bread story, «a shopkeeper sells» the loaf to you, and is paid from the price you pay.
exercise: «Harry said sorry to the shopkeeper and paid with his own pocket money.» Who is the shopkeeper? | A farmer who grows wheat | A child who buys sweets | A driver who delivers bread | *A person who owns or runs a small shop
exercise: Before bread reaches you, a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes and a driver delivers. Which person sells the bread to you? | A driver | A baker | A miller | *A shopkeeper
exercise: Which is the plural of shopkeeper? | shopkeepering | *shopkeepers | shopkeeps | shopkeeper's
test: «The shopkeeper let them stay until the boys had gone and rang Freddie's mum.» What did the shopkeeper do? | Took the boys to school | Went home to bed | *Rang Freddie's mum | Painted the shop green
test: Which of these does a shopkeeper do when you buy something? | Grows the wheat | *Gives you change | Drives the delivery lorry | Grinds the flour
exam: A story calls someone «a kind or grumpy shopkeeper». What do the words kind or grumpy tell you? | *How the shopkeeper behaves | The size of the shop | The type of bread sold | The price of the shop
